.TH DISCORD\-CLI 1 "2026-08-26" "discord\-cli 1.2.1" "discord\-cli Manual"
.SH NAME
discord\-cli \- manage Discord servers and automate Discord from the command
line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
discord\-cli [GLOBAL OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...
discord\-cli \-\-version
discord\-cli \-\-help
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
discord\-cli is a headless, scriptable command\-line interface for Discord.
It authenticates with a Discord bot token, connects to the Discord gateway,
runs exactly one command, prints the result, and exits. There is no
long\-running daemon and no interactive prompt.
.PP
Output is JSON by default so that results can be piped into jq, captured in
CI logs, or consumed by an AI agent without additional parsing glue. Pass
\fB\-\-human\fR to render Rich\-formatted tables for interactive use
instead.
.PP
Every command returns a payload with an \fBok\fR boolean. On success the
payload carries a \fBresult\fR object; on failure it carries an \fBerror\fR
object with a \fBtype\fR and \fBmessage\fR, and the process exits non\-zero.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
These options are accepted by the top\-level command and apply to every
subcommand. They must appear before the command name.
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Show the version and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-token TEXT\fR
Discord bot token. Overrides DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN and .env.
.TP
\fB\-\-guild INTEGER\fR
Target guild ID. Required when the bot is in more than one guild.
.TP
\fB\-\-human\fR
Render human\-readable tables instead of the default JSON output.
.SH COMMANDS
Commands are grouped by the Discord resource they operate on. Each group is
documented in its own section below.
.TP
\fBcategory\fR
Manage channel categories.
.TP
\fBchannel\fR
Manage guild channels.
.TP
