.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBDISCORD_BOT_TOKEN\fR
Discord bot token used to authenticate. Read from the process environment or
from a .env file in the current directory. The \fB\-\-token\fR option takes
precedence over both.
.TP
\fBDISCORD_GUILD_ID\fR
Default guild ID to operate on. The \fB\-\-guild\fR option takes precedence.
Required when the bot is a member of more than one guild.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB\&.env\fR
Read from the current working directory at startup. Used to supply
DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN without exporting it into the shell environment.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\fB0\fR
The command completed successfully and the payload reports ok: true.
.TP
\fB1\fR
The command failed. Causes include a missing or invalid bot token, a missing
guild, channel, role, or member, and any error returned by the Discord API.
The payload reports ok: false with an error object.
.TP
\fB2\fR
The command line could not be parsed, for example an unknown option.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show the current guild's profile as JSON:
.RS 4
.nf
discord\-cli guild info
.fi
.RE
.PP
List channels as a human\-readable table:
.RS 4
.nf
discord\-cli \-\-human channel list
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create a text channel with a topic:
.RS 4
.nf
discord\-cli channel create announcements \-\-type text \\
    \-\-topic "Server announcements"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Send a message to a channel:
.RS 4
.nf
discord\-cli message send 123456789012345678 \-\-content "Deploy finished"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Target a specific guild when the bot is in several:
.RS 4
.nf
discord\-cli \-\-guild 123456789012345678 role list
.fi
.RE
.PP
Export channel history and filter it with jq:
.RS 4
.nf
discord\-cli export channel 123456789012345678 \-\-limit 500 | jq '.result'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Supply the token explicitly instead of via the environment:
